论文题目：
面向复杂火场的AR眼镜与负压爬壁车协同系统
AR Glasses and Negative Pressure Wall-Climbing Vehicle Collaborative System for Complex Fire Scenes


参赛单位：南京师范大学
队伍名称：星火天巡
指导老师：钱伟行
参赛队员：刘元鑫 刘志辉 严鹏旭
完成时间：2026.6.15
  
摘  要
随着超高层建筑、大型地下空间等复杂基础设施的不断增多，现代消防侦察面临着火场环境复杂、危险系数极高的严峻挑战。21世纪以来，计算机软件和硬件技术迅速发展，科技的进步给特种应急救援装备带来了日新月异的变化。但是，目前传统消防侦察设备智能化水平低、实战操作繁琐。
本参赛团队面向复杂火场消防侦察的需求，根据火灾现场危险性的特殊性和救援任务的紧迫性，研制了一款能有效辅助消防员安全高效执行任务的机器人系统。该系统可为消防员的火场侦察提供高稳定性与可靠性的环境感知与智能辅助服务，并具备实时生命体征监测与视觉智能识别功能，该系统是一套功能多样、安全可靠的穿戴式边缘智能消防侦察系统。
本作品包括负压爬壁机器人系统和单兵智能穿戴系统两大主要模块，通过成果集成和技术创新，利用边缘计算多模态信息感知提升系统整体的智能化程度。首先，本作品以负压爬壁机器人作为前端侦察节点，搭载高清摄像头与生命体征传感器，提前深入火场内部探测，不仅能精准检测火灾现场有无生命体，还能通过Wi-Fi将第一视角画面实时串流至智能穿戴端。其次，本作品考虑到消防员实战中的高压信息获取需求，采用单目AR眼镜作为显示终端并搭载RK3588控制芯片与Linux系统，深度接入文字、语音、人物识别等智能模型，在AR眼镜和爬壁车双端均实现了高精度的人体目标检测，辅助消防员在浓烟中快速锁定被困人员。最后，本作品设计了基于手势识别与蓝牙通信的自然交互系统，消防员可通过手势直接控制AR眼镜的UI界面，并利用蓝牙模块实时控制爬壁车的前进与后退，极大释放了消防员的双手。本作品将边缘智能技术与机器人控制方法进行优化与创新，结合具有高性能算力的RK3588平台和单目AR光学显示技术，有效提高了消防侦察系统的态势感知能力与操作的人性化程度，给消防员提供安全可靠、便捷易用的侦察导引和生命搜救服务，为现代消防侦察需求提供了一个完善的解决方案，大幅提高了复杂火场救援的效率与安全性。
本作品立足于一线消防官兵的实际需要，积极响应国家“全面推进应急管理体系和能力现代化”的号召，设计研发了具有自主知识产权和关键技术创新的穿戴式边缘智能消防侦察系统，增进了消防救援队伍的实战保障水平，为特种应急装备领域乃至智能安防领域的发展提供了新思路、新方法。
关键词：消防侦察；AR眼镜；负压爬壁机器人；边缘智能；目标检测  
Abstract
With the increasing number of complex infrastructure such as super high-rise buildings and large underground spaces, modern fire reconnaissance faces the severe challenge of complex fire environments and extremely high hazard levels. Since the 21st century, computer software and hardware technology have developed rapidly, and technological progress has brought rapid changes to special emergency rescue equipment. However, traditional fire reconnaissance equipment currently has low intelligence levels and cumbersome practical operation.
This team developed a robotic system that effectively assists firefighters in safely and efficiently carrying out their tasks to meet the needs of fire reconnaissance in complex fire scenes, tailored to the specificity of fire scene hazards and the urgency of rescue tasks. This system provides firefighters with highly stable and reliable environmental perception and intelligent auxiliary services for fire scene reconnaissance, and features real-time vital sign monitoring and visual intelligent recognition functions. It is a versatile, safe, and reliable wearable edge intelligent fire reconnaissance system.
This work includes two main modules: a negative pressure wall-climbing robot system and a single-soldier intelligent wearable system. Through integration of achievements and technological innovation, it leverages edge computing multimodal information perception to enhance the overall intelligence level of the system. First, this project uses a negative pressure wall-climbing robot as the front-end reconnaissance node, equipped with high-definition cameras and vital sign sensors to probe deep into the fire scene in advance. It can not only accurately detect the presence of life at the fire scene but also stream first-person footage in real time to the smart wearable via Wi-Fi. Second, considering firefighters' high-pressure information acquisition needs in real combat, this work uses monocular AR glasses as display terminals equipped with RK3588 control chips and Linux systems, deeply integrating intelligent models for text, voice, and human recognition. It achieves high-precision human target detection on both the AR glasses and the wall-climbing vehicle, assisting firefighters in quickly locking onto trapped personnel amid thick smoke. Finally, this work designs a natural interaction system based on gesture recognition and Bluetooth communication, allowing firefighters to directly control the AR glasses' UI interface through gestures, and using the Bluetooth module to control the crawling vehicle's forward and backward movement in real time, greatly freeing up firefighters' hands. This work optimizes and innovates edge intelligence technology and robot control methods, combining the high-performance RK3588 platform with monocular AR optical display technology, effectively enhancing the situational awareness and user-friendly operation of fire reconnaissance systems, providing firefighters with safe, reliable, convenient, and easy-to-use reconnaissance guidance and life-saving search and rescue services, offering a comprehensive solution for modern fire reconnaissance needs and significantly improving the efficiency and safety of complex fire rescue operations.
This work is based on the actual needs of frontline firefighters and actively responds to the national call to "comprehensively advance the modernization of emergency management systems and capabilities." It designs and develops a wearable edge intelligent fire reconnaissance system with independent intellectual property rights and key technological innovations, enhancing the practical support level of fire rescue teams and providing new ideas and methods for the development of special emergency equipment and even intelligent security.
Keywords: fire reconnaissance; AR glasses; Negative pressure wall-climbing robot; Edge intelligence; Object detection. 
